1199
01:33:53.812 --> 01:33:54.820
In a flat file,

1200
01:33:54.820 --> 01:34:00.993
Data is stored as plain text, with no formatting like colors or bold type. Each line

1201
01:34:00.993 --> 01:34:07.019
in the file represents one row, with column values separated by a chosen character

1202
01:34:07.019 --> 01:34:12.898
called a delimiter. Usually, the delimiter is a comma, and such files are called

