02:51:55.230 --> 02:52:00.366
Let's begin by exploring a dataset from the popular Nintendo video game, Pokémon.

2097
02:52:00.366 --> 02:52:05.248
The Pokémon game centers around players, called trainers, that try to collect

2098
02:52:05.248 --> 02:52:10.575
fictional animals, called Pokémon. These Pokémon animals roam the fictional universe

2099
02:52:10.575 --> 02:52:15.901
where the game takes place. When a trainer encounters a Pokémon, they try to capture

2100
02:52:15.901 --> 02:52:20.783
that Pokémon to add to their collection. If a trainer successfully captures a

2101
02:52:20.783 --> 02:52:23.890
Pokémon, it is stored in a tool called a Pokédex.

2102
02:52:23.890 --> 02:52:29.543
Each Pokemon comes with its own set of metadata. This metadata contains a name for

