4254
05:43:40.300 --> 05:43:44.720
and use. However, if you installed Python through Anaconda, that will create a

4255
05:43:44.720 --> 05:43:49.367
different copy of Python on top of the native Python that came with your computer.

4256
05:43:49.367 --> 05:43:54.070
Here, we're using Anaconda's Python. One way to interact with Python on the command

4257
05:43:54.070 --> 05:43:58.660
line is within an interactive Python session by typing Python in the terminal and

4258
05:43:58.660 --> 05:44:03.080
pressing Enter. You will know this is a success if you see a printout with the

4259
05:44:03.080 --> 05:44:07.330
Python version, followed by the cursor blinking after three redirect signs.

