05:53:20.887 --> 05:53:26.143
if statements and for loops, and writing functions and learning to schedule scripts

4378
05:53:26.143 --> 05:53:31.400
with cron. Let's first review what bash is and why it matters. Bash stands for born

4379
05:53:31.400 --> 05:53:32.160
again shell.

4380
05:53:32.160 --> 05:53:36.937
and is a pun on it being a replacement for the Bourne shell. It is old, developed in

4381
05:53:36.937 --> 05:53:41.656
the eighties, but it is a very popular shell and often the default for Unix and Mac

4382
05:53:41.656 --> 05:53:46.319
computer systems. Unix systems are the backbone of the internet and servers and so

4383
05:53:46.319 --> 05:53:50.755
important for running large machine learning models and for data pipelines and

4384
05:53:50.755 --> 05:53:55.190
architectures. All major cloud companies have command line interfaces to their

4385
05:53:55.190 --> 05:53:57.010
products. So why bash scripting?

4386
05:53:57.010 --> 05:54:01.549
Rather than copying and pasting your bash commands one by one, you can save and

4387
05:54:01.549 --> 05:54:05.915
execute your program with a single command. You also have access to powerful

4388
05:54:05.915 --> 05:54:10.626
programming constructs mentioned on earlier slides. This course will expect you to

4389
05:54:10.626 --> 05:54:15.394
have certain knowledge, such as understanding the shell or command line. You should

4390
05:54:15.394 --> 05:54:19.875
have used basic commands such as cat, grep, sed, and others before. If you are

4391
05:54:19.875 --> 05:54:24.586
rusty, don't worry, let's revise now. Here are some important shell commands. This

