05:54:47.682 --> 05:54:52.240
or l. and sed does a string replacement using regex pattern matching.

4398
05:54:52.240 --> 05:54:56.485
A few times already we have mentioned pattern matching. Regex, which is an

4399
05:54:56.485 --> 05:55:01.131
abbreviation of regular expressions, are therefore very useful in bash scripting.

4400
05:55:01.131 --> 05:55:05.950
There are a variety of uses for regex in bash scripting, and so it is important that

4401
05:55:05.950 --> 05:55:10.654
you revise this skill and use sites such as regex101.com to test your expressions.

4402
05:55:10.654 --> 05:55:15.415
Let's practice some of those basic shell commands with an example. Imagine that you

4403
05:55:15.415 --> 05:55:19.660
had a text file called fruits.text with the following three lines of data.

4404
05:55:19.660 --> 05:55:24.865
Using the grep command with a letter to match on, we would get this return. That is,

4405
05:55:24.865 --> 05:55:29.947
all the lines containing an A. If we change the letter A for the letter P, then we

4406
05:55:29.947 --> 05:55:34.781
