08:13:08.920 --> 08:13:12.610
Singer does a few more transformations to make better JSON.

6346
08:13:12.610 --> 08:13:17.521
But the details are not that important. Simply use the functionality that is offered

6347
08:13:17.521 --> 08:13:22.198
to you to benefit most. When you would combine the write schema and write record

6348
08:13:22.198 --> 08:13:27.050
functions, you would have a Python module that prints JSON objects to standard out.

6349
08:13:27.050 --> 08:13:31.961
If you also have a single target that can parse these messages, then you have a full

6350
08:13:31.961 --> 08:13:36.813
ingestion pipeline. In this example, we used write records instead of write record.

6351
08:13:36.813 --> 08:13:41.490
It can simply deal with many records compared to the single one of write record.

6352
08:13:41.490 --> 08:13:46.297
We're introducing the target CSV module, which is available on the Python package

