08:18:36.820 --> 08:18:41.850
The actual execution is postponed until we perform an action on this data frame.

6415
08:18:41.850 --> 08:18:47.131
Show is such an action. It will display maximum 20 rows of data in a tabular format.

6416
08:18:47.131 --> 08:18:52.413
We can see the columns of the pricing dataset, but the headers are stored as part of

6417
08:18:52.413 --> 08:18:57.569
the data. Let's fix that. There. By passing the header equals true argument to the

6418
08:18:57.569 --> 08:19:01.970
reader options, the result looks much better. At least on the surface.

6419
08:19:01.970 --> 08:19:07.001
When we inspect the data types of this data frame, we notice that these are all

6420
08:19:07.001 --> 08:19:11.776
strings. We can let Spark infer the schema for us, but keep in mind that in

6421
08:19:11.776 --> 08:19:16.934
production you wouldn't rely on incorrectly inferred data types, so you typically

