08:22:48.240 --> 08:22:53.119
For that, we use the fillNA method, which optionally accepts a list of column names

6467
08:22:53.119 --> 08:22:57.762
as input. Only those columns will be affected, as you can see. People often put

6468
08:22:57.762 --> 08:23:02.641
placeholders for fields they don't know the value of. In this example, someone gave

6469
08:23:02.641 --> 08:23:07.402
an unrealistic date for the end of Alice's employment contract. Such placeholders

6470
08:23:07.402 --> 08:23:12.045
are bad for analytics purposes. In most cases, it's better to have unknown data

