10:54:14.720 --> 10:54:19.252
It's important to keep track of the views in your database. To get all the views in

8346
10:54:19.252 --> 10:54:23.729
your database, you can run a query on the informationschema.views table. Note that

8347
10:54:23.729 --> 10:54:28.152
this command is specific to PostgreSQL. If you're using another DBMS, look at its

8348
10:54:28.152 --> 10:54:32.684
documentation to find the equivalent command. If you run this command, you will get

8349
10:54:32.684 --> 10:54:37.270
a long list of views. That's because DBMSs have their own built-in views. To exclude

8350
