15:02:54.036 --> 15:02:59.197
can use the cast or the convert functions we already learned in the previous

11489
15:02:59.197 --> 15:02:59.740
chapter.

11490
15:02:59.740 --> 15:03:05.337
Within the two functions, we have to specify into which type we want to convert the

11491
15:03:05.337 --> 15:03:11.001
rating column. In these cases, we are going to convert the type of the rating column

11492
15:03:11.001 --> 15:03:16.598
into a float number. Running any of these queries, we will get the expected result.

11493
15:03:16.598 --> 15:03:21.520
It is the content of the series table with ratings on a scale of 0 to 10.

11494
15:03:21.520 --> 15:03:27.080
Additionally, if we also want to calculate the average of the rating column, we will

11495
15:03:27.080 --> 15:03:32.310
have to use the convert or cast functions for that operation. As we can see, we

11496
15:03:32.310 --> 15:03:37.870
correctly got the expected result. Let's practice! In this lesson, we will learn how

11497
15:03:37.870 --> 15:03:43.166
to match patterns using SQL Server. Let's start by illustrating pattern matching

11498
15:03:43.166 --> 15:03:48.395
with an example. In the series table, there is a column that stores the contact

11499
15:03:48.395 --> 15:03:50.050
numbers of the producers.

11500
15:03:50.050 --> 15:03:56.427
Suppose that the contact numbers must have this format. It is 3 digits followed by a

11501
15:03:56.427 --> 15:04:02.728
hyphen, then another 3 digits followed by another hyphen, and finally 4 digits. The

11502
15:04:02.728 --> 15:04:09.105
first and the 4 digits must be numbers between 2 and 9, and the rest numbers between

